  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "In the expansion of $\\left(x+\\frac{a}{x}\\right)^8$, the constant term is 5670. Find $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=\\pm3$.\n\nThe constant term is $\\binom{8}{4}a^4=70a^4$, so $a^4=81$.",
      "worked": "The general term is\n$$\\begin{align*}T_{k+1}&=\\binom{8}{k}x^{8-k}\\left(\\frac{a}{x}\\right)^k\\\\T_{k+1}&=\\binom{8}{k}a^kx^{8-2k}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the constant term, $8-2k=0$, so $k=4$. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}70a^4&=5670\\\\a^4&=81\\\\a&=\\pm3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
